    creates a sample set if run with the:
    $env:PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF = "expandable_segments:True"; .\venv\Scripts\python.exe .\sample_vqa_GPU.py --model_path diffuvqa/config/ema_0.9999_000500.pt --batch_size 1 --split test --dataset slake --data_dir datasets --image_dir datasets/slake/imgs --seed2 110 --step 50
    command
    
    Critical Sampling Command Fix
    The key parameter that fixed everything:
    
    --step 50
    
    After applying the below changes to the training_args.json file
    
    {
      "diffusion_steps": 1000,        // Reduced from 2500
      "timestep_respacing": [50],     // Added proper respacing
      "log_interval": 25,             // Reduced logging frequency
      "save_interval": 100            // Reduced save frequency
    }
    
    Memory efficiency: Fewer diffusion steps (1000 vs 2500) = less GPU memory for storing intermediate states
    Timestep respacing: [50] creates a compressed diffusion schedule, using only 50 key timesteps instead of all 1000
    Reduced I/O overhead: Less frequent logging/saving operations free up GPU memory and reduce disk bottlenecks
    
    Why It Previously Failed
    Memory Issues:
    
    Large diffusion steps (2500) + full timestep schedule = massive GPU memory requirements
    Invalid step calculations caused memory allocation failures
    Frequent logging/saving operations caused memory fragmentation
    
    Summary
    The fix was essentially mathematical correctness + memory optimization:
    
    --step 50: Fixed the core division-by-zero error in timestep calculation
    timestep_respacing=[50]: Compressed the diffusion schedule for efficiency

